 ### [Hierarchical Density Adaptation](4868-hierarchical-density-adaptation.md)
-A variant that derives coarse density by convolving a dense feature grid with a non-learnable kernel, avoiding dedicated coarse grid allocation.
+A sampling strategy for direct volume ray casting that generates a coarse density estimate from a dense feature grid on the fly to guide importance sampling for fine samples. It solves the problem of missing thin or high-frequency surface details when sampling directly from a dense grid, which occurs if coarse sample points fall between grid cells containing significant geometry. Unlike sibling methods that maintain a dedicated, pre-computed coarse grid or train a separate coarse network, this method derives the coarse density by convolving the existing dense density grid with a non-learnable kernel, thereby avoiding additional memory allocation for coarse structures while ensuring robust surface detection. It is chosen when memory is constrained or when avoiding the overhead of training a separate coarse network is preferred.
 
